From: xenocideend (with Claude Opus 5.5) <xenocideend@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_pm8150b_charger: prefer the battery's
 charge voltage and always cap the charge current

0018 clamps the float voltage to 3.6-4.45 V. Two gaps are left: a battery
node that sets constant-charge-voltage-max-microvolt below the design max
still charges to the design max, and a constant-charge-current-max-microamp
above 3 A goes straight to the register. Use the lower of the two voltages
and cap the charge current at 3 A in every case. No SM8250 board changes
value today.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8150b_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8150b_charger.c
@@ -1140,7 +1140,12 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc,
 				     "Failed to init status change work\n");
 
-	rc = clamp(chip->batt_info->voltage_max_design_uv, 3600000, 4450000);
+	/* the battery's own charge voltage when its lower than the design max */
+	rc = chip->batt_info->voltage_max_design_uv;
+	if (chip->batt_info->constant_charge_voltage_max_uv > 0 &&
+	    (rc <= 0 || chip->batt_info->constant_charge_voltage_max_uv < rc))
+		rc = chip->batt_info->constant_charge_voltage_max_uv;
+	rc = clamp(rc, 3600000, 4450000);
 	rc = (rc - 3600000) / 10000;
 	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + FLOAT_VOLTAGE_CFG,
 				FLOAT_VOLTAGE_SETTING_MASK, rc);
@@ -1149,7 +1154,8 @@
 
 	rc = chip->batt_info->constant_charge_current_max_ua;
 	if (rc <= 0)
-		rc = min(chip->batt_info->charge_full_design_uah / 2, 3000000);
+		rc = chip->batt_info->charge_full_design_uah / 2;
+	rc = min(rc, 3000000);		/* never above 3 A, whatever the battery node says */
 	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap,
 				chip->base + FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_CFG,
 				FAST_CHARGE_CURRENT_SETTING_MASK, rc / 50000);
